# Agent tasks session audit (every ticket)

**Mandatory on every Cursor agent session / ticket** — not optional, not handback-only.

Directory: `.agent_tasks/<session-id>/` where `<session-id>` is the last segment of `{{VSCODE_TARGET_SESSION_LOG}}` (or a stable ticket slug if that var is unset). **Gitignored** — do not commit these files.

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `command.md` | Append-only log of **every Shell tool command** run on the machine, each with a short what/why |
| `lesson_learnt.md` | Ongoing append of non-obvious lessons learnt during implementation |

## When to write

- **`command.md`** — after each Shell tool use (Make/git/gh/docker/pytest/curl/etc.), append in the **same turn** (batch before handback only if many; prefer soon after running).
- **`lesson_learnt.md`** — whenever something non-obvious is learned (**ongoing**), not only at handback.

## Forbidden under `.agent_tasks/`

Do **not** create `plan.md`, `todo.md`, `lessons.md`, `review.stamp`, or `review-feedback.md`. Plans stay in Cursor plan UI / chat. No file-based review gate.

## Templates

```markdown
# Commands

- `git status` — inspect working tree before branching
- `make test-agent-stop` — verify agent-edited tests before handback
```

```markdown
# Lessons learnt

- <date or turn>: <one lesson>
```

## Depth / handback

Templates and workflow wiring: `.cursor/skills/how-to-code/SKILL.md` § Task files. Handback incomplete if Shell commands ran this session and `command.md` was never updated.
